{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>When he spoke</b> — From his speech the nations were afraid, and the word רתת has a cognate only in Aramaic. And R. Moses the Cohen interpreted: this refers to Jeroboam, who was from Ephraim, like 'this is Jeroboam son of Joash,' as I will yet explain." "<b>He exalted himself</b> — That his kingdom was exalted in Israel, for he ruled over the ten tribes." "<b>And he became guilty, and he died</b> — He is accounted as dead. And furthermore: for Abijah killed his entire camp."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The phrase 'like \"this is Jeroboam son of Joash\"' likely alludes to a verse citation (2 Kings 14:23 or Amos 7:9), but none is given explicitly in the text."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:06.908213690Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}